        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">In 1984 the Canadian Labour Congress set this day aside for workers killed, hurt, or made sick by their jobs, and in 1991 Parliament made it official. Flags fly at half-mast, and many workplaces keep a moment of silence at 11 a.m. Many other countries now mark the same day.</value>
